  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-08-27T20:44:02.017Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It's confusing and misleading that my friends appear in \"Private Worlds\" when they are actually in the Friends-Only instance of someone you don't have befriended.\n\nIt's especially bad if that friend has the Join Me status, because you will expect it to automatically accept your join request, only to not actually get an invite because they weren't truly in a private world.\n\nIt's cumbersome to send a request for an invite to a friend who's in a Friends-Only world, where my friend then has to ask the instance owner to find my username and friend request me, or somehow tell me who to send a friend request to.\n\nIt'd be much simpler if I could just send a friend request to that instance owner directly. The instance owner can then sort out with my friend about why he just got a random friend request.\n\nPerhaps it doesn't even need to be a friend request - let me send a join request to the instance owner without having to friend them. This would make Friends-Only seem similar to how private worlds already are, but instead of requesting the invites from your friends, you're requesting off of instance owners and don't necessarily have to befriend them.",
